{"id":"issachar-the-tribe-of","name":"Issachar, The Tribe Of","aliases":["Issachar"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:issachar-the-tribe-of"],"types":[{"type":"person","from":"UBS: Names of People"},{"type":"group","from":"UBS: Names of Groups"},{"type":"place","from":"UBS: Names of Locations"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["torrey"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Issachar","text":"Hired (Gen. 30:18). “God hath given me,” said Leah, “my hire (Heb. sekhari)...and she called his name Issachar.” He was Jacob’s ninth son, and was born in Padan-aram (comp. 28:2). He had four sons at the going down into Egypt (46:13; Num. 26:23, 25). Issachar, Tribe of, during the journey through the wilderness, along with Judah and Zebulun (Num. 2:5), marched on the east of the tabernacle. This tribe contained 54,400 fighting men when the census was taken at Sinai. After the entrance into the Promised Land, this tribe was one of the six which stood on Gerizim during the ceremony of the blessing and cursing (Deut. 27:12). The allotment of Issachar is described in Josh. 19:17-23. It included the plain of Esdraelon (=Jezreel), which was and still is the richest portion of Palestine (Deut. 33:18, 19; 1 Chr. 12:40). The prophetic blessing pronounced by Jacob on Issachar corresponds with …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3485","lemma":"יִשָּׂשכָר","xlit":"Yissâˢkâr","gloss":"Jissaskar, a son of Jacob","kjv":"Issachar","count":24,"share":0.59},{"strong":"H4940","lemma":"מִשְׁפָּחָה","xlit":"mishpâchâh","gloss":"a family","kjv":"family, kind","count":7,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H4294","lemma":"מַטֶּה","xlit":"maṭṭeh","gloss":"a branch","kjv":"rod, staff, tribe","count":6,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":20,"share":0.49},{"strong":"H3967","lemma":"מֵאָה","xlit":"mêʼâh","gloss":"a hundred","kjv":"hundred, -th), sixscore","count":6,"sha